<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καστόρειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Castor</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ Κ. μέλος</span> a martial song, set to the
			flute, used in celebrating victories in the horse or chariot races,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.69
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Κ. ὕμνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>I.</u>
					1.16
				</span></i>
			; also, of a battle-march, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.1140c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				p.25
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καστόρειος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασσ-όριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i>of
				the beaver</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάστωρ; αἷμα</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.24
			</span></i>:—esp. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καστόρειον</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κασσ-όριον</span></b> , τό, <i>castor</i>,
			secretion found in the body of the beaver, used in medicine, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.Lond.
				37.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1088.27
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.55a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phlp.
				<u>in GC</u>
				65.29
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
